  "summary": {
    "intent": "Drive a set of reviewed PRs on the caliper repo to merge-readiness, specifically fixing two silent-wrong-output bugs (a cached checker outage and a persisted read failure) via subagent workers and code review.",
    "outcome": "Branch fix/degraded-results-are-not-kept (#527) fixed both bugs with failing-first tests and passing gates, but the code review found real gaps, so a worker was dispatched to complete the fix across all read paths before the PR body is published.",
    "learnings": {
      "repo": [
        "Settled::Degraded outcomes must never be cached; their warning has to appear on every affected answer, but needs a short-lived negative cache or backoff to avoid re-asking an unavailable checker per request.",
        "An unreadable file must be treated as a cut (explicit result), not as an absence; a degraded marker needs to be carried into the DependencyLayer that later loads inherit, or write_index can persist poisoned answers.",
        "Absence must not be read as evidence: 'no components and no fallbacks' does not mean 'checker unavailable', so SemanticOutcome needs an explicit unavailable marker.",
        "Reading a file outside the OnceLock init in parse_source multiplies I/O under rayon concurrency; reads should be single-flight per file.",
        "kept.rs persists Rejected fallbacks and lib.rs:838 holds the panic/STOPPED fallback; both need a transient marker so they are not cached or saved.",
        "Gates for this repo: lint, nextest, checker-lane, gate_harness determinism and memory, plus output identical to origin/main on mantine and chakra."
      ],
      "code": [
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs",
          "line": 1405,
          "finding": "The unreadable guard only stops write_index; the flag lives on one Loader and is not carried into the layer inherited by later loads."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs",
          "line": 241,
          "finding": "Degraded is never cached or joined, so a permanently unavailable checker is re-asked and re-warned on every request."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/pipeline/semantic_hook.rs",
          "line": 392,
          "finding": "read_outcome treats empty components and fallbacks as 'checker unavailable', which also matches a real outcome lacking the asked key."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs",
          "line": 535,
          "finding": "parse_source reads outside the OnceLock init, so concurrent callers each read the same file."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/core/src/dependency_types.rs",
          "line": 905,
          "finding": "scan calls self.read(file)? then parse_source with .ok().flatten(), hiding Unreadable as 'declares nothing'."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/lib.rs",
          "line": 430,
          "finding": "reroot leaks old and newly created snapshots when it fails part-way (already-merged code)."
        },
        {
          "path": "crates/semantic/src/asked.rs",
